WEBVTT

1
00:52:36.194 --> 00:52:38.194
Good morning!

2
00:52:41.474 --> 00:52:44.194
Good morning! Isn't it nice to see each other?

3
00:52:47.794 --> 00:52:52.434
You receive greetings from Tim and Vanessa, and from the children.

4
00:52:52.434 --> 00:52:54.434
Hi!

5
00:52:54.434 --> 00:52:56.434
And they are still enjoying their vacation.

6
00:52:57.554 --> 00:53:03.714
Also, of course, it's wonderful for all the people who are on vacation, or maybe there are people here on vacation.

7
00:53:03.714 --> 00:53:07.714
Who is on vacation, and here visiting? Hello!

8
00:53:09.714 --> 00:53:11.714
How nice!

9
00:53:11.714 --> 00:53:15.714
This morning I get to share something, to present.

10
00:53:15.714 --> 00:53:19.714
And let's first see which text I have for that.

11
00:53:23.714 --> 00:53:29.714
Jesus came six days before the Passover to Bethany, where Lazarus lived.

12
00:53:29.714 --> 00:53:33.714
Lazarus was the man who had died and was made alive again by Jesus.

13
00:53:33.714 --> 00:53:37.714
They prepared a meal for him, Martha served him.

14
00:53:37.714 --> 00:53:41.714
Martha is the sister of Lazarus.

15
00:53:41.714 --> 00:53:45.714
Lazarus was sitting at the table with him along with other people.

16
00:53:47.714 --> 00:53:57.714
Mary took a pound of expensive perfume, pure nard oil, and anointed Jesus' feet with it.

17
00:53:57.714 --> 00:54:01.714
Then she wiped his feet with her hair.

18
00:54:01.714 --> 00:54:07.714
The wonderful fragrance of the perfume was noticeable throughout the whole house.

19
00:54:07.714 --> 00:54:13.714
So far this part. This story is found in all four gospels.

20
00:54:13.714 --> 00:54:21.714
Each gospel, of course, with different details and different points to emphasize.

21
00:54:21.714 --> 00:54:27.714
But what I want to talk about today, and this is so beautiful, is that worship is giving.

22
00:54:27.714 --> 00:54:33.714
And giving is worship. You can call it both ways.

23
00:54:33.714 --> 00:54:39.714
Because what she is doing here is she is giving that oil.

24
00:54:39.714 --> 00:54:41.714
And you could say, yes, like that.

25
00:54:41.714 --> 00:54:49.714
Well, a pound of oil is stated elsewhere to be worth 300 silver coins.

26
00:54:49.714 --> 00:54:53.714
And 300 silver coins was about a year's salary.

27
00:54:53.714 --> 00:55:03.714
So what she is giving there is simply pouring a bottle of oil worth a year's salary over his feet.

28
00:55:03.714 --> 00:55:08.714
And kissing his feet. And drying them with her hair.

29
00:55:08.714 --> 00:55:12.714
And then you could say, yes, but why then?

30
00:55:12.714 --> 00:55:18.714
Well, that is not stated in this passage, but it is in another passage.

31
00:55:19.714 --> 00:55:23.714
She had done things in her life that were unacceptable.

32
00:55:23.714 --> 00:55:26.714
But she was forgiven.

33
00:55:26.714 --> 00:55:30.714
All those things were behind her.

34
00:55:30.714 --> 00:55:35.714
Jesus forgives what you have done wrong in your life.

35
00:55:35.714 --> 00:55:39.714
He restores your life. He makes your life new again.

36
00:55:39.714 --> 00:55:42.714
He gives you a new start and a new chance.

37
00:55:43.714 --> 00:55:49.714
And from that gratitude and from that joy, she wants to give worship.

38
00:55:49.714 --> 00:55:51.714
She wants to give.

39
00:55:51.714 --> 00:55:54.714
And whether that is oil on the feet.

40
00:55:54.714 --> 00:55:58.714
Or whether that is a financial gift like we do here.

41
00:55:58.714 --> 00:56:03.714
Whether it's singing a song that truly comes from your innermost being.

42
00:56:03.714 --> 00:56:07.714
When we sing a song, you can also be on your bike and sing a song.

43
00:56:07.714 --> 00:56:09.714
Thoughtlessly.

44
00:56:09.714 --> 00:56:11.714
That is not necessarily worship.

45
00:56:11.714 --> 00:56:15.714
Worship is giving from your innermost being.

46
00:56:15.714 --> 00:56:21.714
And that applies to worship in singing, but it also applies to worship in giving financially.

47
00:56:21.714 --> 00:56:28.714
That also applies to worship participating in the church with the things that need to be done.

48
00:56:28.714 --> 00:56:32.714
If it comes from your innermost being and you do it from your heart.

49
00:56:32.714 --> 00:56:35.714
To give it to Him, to honor Him.

50
00:56:35.714 --> 00:56:37.714
Then that is worship.

51
00:56:38.714 --> 00:56:41.714
And you know, everything you do in your life.

52
00:56:41.714 --> 00:56:47.714
Of course, you just go from one moment to the next in your day.

53
00:56:47.714 --> 00:56:51.714
And I really compartmentalize my life completely.

54
00:56:51.714 --> 00:56:53.714
I am such a structured person.

55
00:56:53.714 --> 00:56:59.714
You know, sometimes I don't think about this part being worship as well.

56
00:56:59.714 --> 00:57:03.714
And we often think, oh now we have sung songs, that part was worship.

57
00:57:03.714 --> 00:57:05.714
Oh now Debbie is coming, now it’s about giving.

58
00:57:06.714 --> 00:57:12.714
Yes, no, but you can be aware that all of that is worship.

59
00:57:12.714 --> 00:57:17.714
That if you do your best to keep your house nice and tidy.

60
00:57:17.714 --> 00:57:20.714
That it is also for His honor.

61
00:57:20.714 --> 00:57:21.714
So also worship.

62
00:57:21.714 --> 00:57:26.714
When you tell your children about the love of God, that is also worship.

63
00:57:26.714 --> 00:57:33.714
So when you are on that bike singing a song and it comes from your heart, that is also worship.

64
00:57:33.714 --> 00:57:38.714
And the trees in the field will join in, says the Bible.

65
00:57:38.714 --> 00:57:43.714
So I want to challenge you to give from your heart.

66
00:57:43.714 --> 00:57:48.714
From that true worship, you can give from there. Amen.

67
00:57:55.714 --> 00:57:58.714
I also have two really nice things to share.

68
00:57:58.714 --> 00:58:02.714
Namely, the summer camps are coming up.

69
00:58:03.714 --> 00:58:05.714
Yay!

70
00:58:06.714 --> 00:58:11.714
I don't think everyone was very enthusiastic, but well, the summer camps are coming up.

71
00:58:12.714 --> 00:58:15.714
And what is very important.

72
00:58:15.714 --> 00:58:24.714
If you haven't signed up your child, your teenager, or your husband for the camps yet, do that quickly.

73
00:58:24.714 --> 00:58:31.714
Because today is July 28th and the forms close on the 31st.

74
00:58:31.714 --> 00:58:33.714
So you have three days left.

75
00:58:33.714 --> 00:58:39.714
So quickly sign up your children or your teenagers or your husband for the camps.

76
00:58:39.714 --> 00:58:43.714
And it's also very nice to get the finances sorted out right away.

77
00:58:43.714 --> 00:58:48.714
Because that is simply necessary for all the purchases in advance.

78
00:58:48.714 --> 00:58:50.714
And then one more nice little thing.

79
00:58:50.714 --> 00:58:55.714
There is still a congratulatory card for Ivan and Sadis.

80
00:58:55.714 --> 00:58:57.714
They have had a baby.

81
00:58:57.714 --> 00:58:59.714
They live in Spain.

82
00:58:59.714 --> 00:59:02.714
Our church is connected in friendship with their church.

83
00:59:02.714 --> 00:59:04.714
They have had a baby.

84
00:59:04.714 --> 00:59:06.714
It is a fantastic miracle.

85
00:59:06.714 --> 00:59:09.714
So if you want to congratulate them on that card for a moment.

86
00:59:09.714 --> 00:59:12.714
Today it is still there, after that it will be gone.

87
00:59:12.714 --> 00:59:14.714
Then we will take it to them.

88
00:59:14.714 --> 00:59:18.714
So be sure to congratulate them for a moment.

89
00:59:19.714 --> 00:59:22.714
I may invite you, Bram.

90
00:59:22.714 --> 00:59:24.714
He will share the Word with us.

91
00:59:24.714 --> 00:59:26.714
And I am very curious.

92
00:59:26.714 --> 00:59:30.714
So I would say, open your ears and your heart where we open it.

93
00:59:30.714 --> 00:59:32.714
To receive.

94
00:59:41.714 --> 00:59:44.714
Thank you. Good morning everyone.

95
00:59:46.714 --> 00:59:50.714
Wild De Huis is here.

96
00:59:51.714 --> 00:59:53.714
Our theme for the year.

97
00:59:55.714 --> 01:00:02.714
And that is primarily, build the church.

98
01:00:03.714 --> 01:00:09.714
Make sure the church is healthy, strong, good, beautiful.

99
01:00:10.714 --> 01:00:21.714
For the church is to represent the light of Jesus Christ, to be in this world.

100
01:00:22.714 --> 01:00:26.714
The church is important to God.

101
01:00:27.714 --> 01:00:34.714
Jesus, when he was hanging on the cross, he said, I look forward to being with my brothers.

102
01:00:34.714 --> 01:00:37.714
After his resurrection, that is the church.

103
01:00:38.714 --> 01:00:46.714
But as most of you already know, we are of course also working on a construction project.

104
01:00:46.714 --> 01:00:49.714
We are in the project development phase.

105
01:00:49.714 --> 01:00:51.714
We have made a plan.

106
01:00:52.714 --> 01:00:54.714
I will come back to that later.

107
01:00:56.714 --> 01:01:04.714
And if that is our theme for the year, I thought, there are various construction projects in the Bible.

108
01:01:05.714 --> 01:01:08.714
Shall we take a look at one?

109
01:01:08.714 --> 01:01:12.714
Shall we go on a journey with Nehemiah?

110
01:01:12.714 --> 01:01:14.714
Who knows Nehemiah already?

111
01:01:14.714 --> 01:01:18.714
Okay, then you don't have to... No, I won't say that.

112
01:01:19.714 --> 01:01:22.714
No, you know, there is always something new in the Word.

113
01:01:22.714 --> 01:01:28.714
I was preparing this and you just see new things and that is fantastic.

114
01:01:29.714 --> 01:01:31.714
We are going on a journey with Nehemiah.

115
01:01:34.714 --> 01:01:38.714
And then we are around the year...

116
01:01:38.714 --> 01:01:40.714
Is that correct?

117
01:01:40.714 --> 01:01:45.714
Around the year, yes, let's say, 450 before Christ.

118
01:01:47.714 --> 01:01:53.714
And about 150 years earlier, things went terribly wrong.

119
01:01:57.714 --> 01:02:05.714
The Babylonian king Nebuchadnezzar conquered the land of Judah.

120
01:02:06.714 --> 01:02:12.714
And in different groups, he took the entire population away.

121
01:02:12.714 --> 01:02:17.714
Well, the entire population that could do something, that had something to say.

122
01:02:17.714 --> 01:02:22.714
He left the poor, the downtrodden behind.

123
01:02:22.714 --> 01:02:24.714
They couldn't organize anything anyway.

124
01:02:24.714 --> 01:02:26.714
They posed no threat to him.

125
01:02:26.714 --> 01:02:30.714
Just mess around, was the thought.

126
01:02:30.714 --> 01:02:33.714
People didn't have much sympathy for others at that time.

127
01:02:33.714 --> 01:02:37.714
There was no such thing as human rights or anything like that, it really didn't exist.

128
01:02:38.714 --> 01:02:40.714
It was brutal.

129
01:02:41.714 --> 01:02:45.714
You can read in the Bible what happened to the king at that time.

130
01:02:48.714 --> 01:02:50.714
Something about gouging out eyes and such.

131
01:02:54.714 --> 01:03:00.714
So the people were taken away to Babylon.

132
01:03:00.714 --> 01:03:05.714
To Babylon, really a few months of travel.

133
01:03:08.714 --> 01:03:13.714
The city and the temple were plundered, oh terrible.

134
01:03:13.714 --> 01:03:21.714
The place where the holiness of God is, was plundered, was destroyed.

135
01:03:21.714 --> 01:03:24.714
The city was set on fire.

136
01:03:25.714 --> 01:03:31.714
So the people who were left behind had no means of existence.

137
01:03:31.714 --> 01:03:33.714
It was poverty.

138
01:03:34.714 --> 01:03:38.714
And they were the mockery of the surroundings.

139
01:03:41.714 --> 01:03:49.714
70 years later, the Persians conquer the Babylonian Empire.

140
01:03:49.714 --> 01:03:51.714
So now we get the Persian Empire.

141
01:03:51.714 --> 01:03:53.714
Perhaps you have heard something about it during history lessons.

142
01:03:55.714 --> 01:04:00.714
Under King Cyrus, the people received permission to return.

143
01:04:00.714 --> 01:04:03.714
And the first groups went back under the leadership of Zerubbabel.

144
01:04:03.714 --> 01:04:11.714
But you have to imagine, in 70 years' time, it wasn't that they were imprisoned or anything.

145
01:04:11.714 --> 01:04:20.714
They were simply taken away, dropped here, and they built their existence there.

146
01:04:20.714 --> 01:04:27.714
There were probably Jewish neighborhoods, where they could have their own lives together a bit.

147
01:04:27.714 --> 01:04:30.714
But they had built their existence there.

148
01:04:31.714 --> 01:04:33.714
You had your job there.

149
01:04:33.714 --> 01:04:35.714
The children went to school there.

150
01:04:36.714 --> 01:04:38.714
Not so different from today, you know.

151
01:04:41.714 --> 01:04:46.714
So the step to go back to a dilapidated city.

152
01:04:47.714 --> 01:04:49.714
Where you don't know how to earn your bread.

153
01:04:49.714 --> 01:04:52.714
Where you don't know what life looks like there.

154
01:04:54.714 --> 01:04:56.714
That is a step you need faith for.

155
01:04:57.714 --> 01:04:59.714
That is a step you need vision for.

156
01:05:00.714 --> 01:05:08.714
Because God had said, this is the place, this is where my people belong.

157
01:05:08.714 --> 01:05:14.714
This is where the temple is supposed to stand.

158
01:05:14.714 --> 01:05:21.714
The temple that at that moment truly was the center of all religious life.

159
01:05:25.714 --> 01:05:31.714
Different groups went back, but it remained problematic there in Jerusalem.

160
01:05:31.714 --> 01:05:43.714
No, the temple was rebuilt, but it remained a hassle.

161
01:05:43.714 --> 01:05:48.714
It did not come to rest, it did not come to development.

162
01:05:48.714 --> 01:05:55.714
And in the meantime, we are about ninety years further along after those first groups.

163
01:05:55.714 --> 01:05:59.714
Do you know how long ninety years is? What did it look like here ninety years ago?

164
01:06:00.714 --> 01:06:03.714
Back then, horse-drawn carriages were still driving through the streets.

165
01:06:04.714 --> 01:06:06.714
Oh yes, and the very first cars.

166
01:06:07.714 --> 01:06:11.714
Those cars from the thirties, those colossal stinky things.

167
01:06:11.714 --> 01:06:12.714
Oh, sorry.

168
01:06:13.714 --> 01:06:15.714
Excuse me for the enthusiasts.

169
01:06:20.714 --> 01:06:22.714
Generations had passed over it.

170
01:06:23.714 --> 01:06:28.714
And all that time, generations simply settled in Babylon.

171
01:06:30.714 --> 01:06:34.714
And one of those people is Nehemiah.

172
01:06:36.714 --> 01:06:42.714
Nehemiah grew up under the Persian Empire.

173
01:06:43.714 --> 01:06:47.714
He has a high position as an official.

174
01:06:47.714 --> 01:06:49.714
He studied hard.

175
01:06:50.714 --> 01:06:55.714
And we will start at the beginning of Nehemiah.

176
01:06:56.714 --> 01:07:02.714
Do you know what is so beautiful? We really have his own account.

177
01:07:03.714 --> 01:07:06.714
He simply wrote down his own story.

178
01:07:06.714 --> 01:07:08.714
When we come to our Bible.

179
01:07:09.714 --> 01:07:14.714
And that is the story of how God led Nehemiah to a special task.

180
01:07:16.714 --> 01:07:20.714
This is the story of Nehemiah, the son of Hachalia.

181
01:07:21.714 --> 01:07:23.714
My story begins in the month of Kislev.

182
01:07:23.714 --> 01:07:27.714
When Ataxerxes was the king of Persia.

183
01:07:28.714 --> 01:07:32.714
I worked for the king in the citadel of Susa, the government center.

184
01:07:34.714 --> 01:07:39.714
Hanani, one of my brothers, came from Judah with a number of Judeans to me.

185
01:07:41.714 --> 01:07:43.714
His brother lived in Judah, therefore.

186
01:07:44.714 --> 01:07:48.714
His brother had returned to Jerusalem and visited him.

187
01:07:48.714 --> 01:07:51.714
I asked how it was going with the people who had been left behind in Judah.

188
01:07:52.714 --> 01:07:55.714
When all the others had been captured and taken to Babylon.

189
01:07:57.714 --> 01:07:59.714
I also asked them how it was with Jerusalem.

190
01:08:00.714 --> 01:08:03.714
They answered, and let's take a look at that together.

191
01:08:05.714 --> 01:08:09.714
The people who have remained in Judah are in great trouble.

192
01:08:10.714 --> 01:08:12.714
They are being killed by everyone.

193
01:08:12.714 --> 01:08:16.714
The people who have remained in Judah are in great trouble.

194
01:08:17.714 --> 01:08:19.714
They are being mocked by everyone.

195
01:08:20.714 --> 01:08:22.714
Jerusalem is also in a bad state.

196
01:08:23.714 --> 01:08:28.714
The wall has been broken down and the gates have been burned.

197
01:08:32.714 --> 01:08:34.714
And then Nehemiah continues.

198
01:08:34.714 --> 01:08:39.714
When I heard this, I sat down in sorrow and wept.

199
01:08:43.714 --> 01:08:45.714
For days I was deeply saddened.

200
01:08:46.714 --> 01:08:49.714
I ate nothing and prayed to the God of heaven.

201
01:08:51.714 --> 01:08:53.714
He is completely out of sorts.

202
01:08:54.714 --> 01:08:56.714
He can no longer function.

203
01:08:57.714 --> 01:08:59.714
His whole daily life is at a standstill.

204
01:09:00.714 --> 01:09:02.714
This affects him so much.

205
01:09:04.714 --> 01:09:08.714
And that is actually lesson number one.

206
01:09:09.714 --> 01:09:15.714
Everything that happens next in this whole book begins with him being touched in his heart.

207
01:09:16.714 --> 01:09:19.714
That he is touched in his heart for the cause of God.

208
01:09:22.714 --> 01:09:27.714
That he does not simply say, oh well, these things happen and everyday life goes on.

209
01:09:28.714 --> 01:09:31.714
Oh, we watch the news and we see yet another thing on the news.

210
01:09:32.714 --> 01:09:33.714
Life just goes on.

211
01:09:33.714 --> 01:09:37.714
No, of course, I understand. You can't take everything to heart one hundred percent.

212
01:09:38.714 --> 01:09:42.714
But here the heart of Nehemiah is touched for the cause of God.

213
01:09:43.714 --> 01:09:48.714
His heart is touched for his brothers who are in distress.

214
01:09:50.714 --> 01:09:54.714
His heart is touched by the Holy Spirit of God.

215
01:09:56.714 --> 01:09:57.714
For that is how God works.

216
01:09:57.714 --> 01:09:58.714
For that is how God works.

217
01:10:00.714 --> 01:10:04.714
And everything begins with what lives in our heart.

218
01:10:08.714 --> 01:10:11.714
So here passion arises. Here you see involvement.

219
01:10:12.714 --> 01:10:13.714
Here you see compassion.

220
01:10:15.714 --> 01:10:21.714
Here you see the desire that this cannot exist.

221
01:10:22.714 --> 01:10:25.714
This is the temple of God.

222
01:10:25.714 --> 01:10:27.714
These are the people of God.

223
01:10:33.714 --> 01:10:34.714
Then comes the first action.

224
01:10:37.714 --> 01:10:39.714
What do you think the first action is?

225
01:10:40.714 --> 01:10:45.714
Ah, we are going to make plans, we are going to stock up, we are going to hold a fundraising campaign.

226
01:10:46.714 --> 01:10:47.714
Right?

227
01:10:51.714 --> 01:10:52.714
Almost right.

228
01:10:56.714 --> 01:11:01.714
Nehemiah says, Lord God of heaven, great and mighty God, he is going to pray.

229
01:11:02.714 --> 01:11:06.714
And what he prays, pay attention to what he is praying now.

230
01:11:08.714 --> 01:11:14.714
He recognizes God as great, mighty, wonderful.

231
01:11:15.714 --> 01:11:18.714
It is not God's fault, the misery we have here is not God's fault.

232
01:11:19.714 --> 01:11:20.714
God is good.

233
01:11:21.714 --> 01:11:22.714
God has a good plan.

234
01:11:22.714 --> 01:11:25.714
God has a good plan for you and for me.

235
01:11:26.714 --> 01:11:33.714
God has a plan that, he says, you know, elsewhere John writes,

236
01:11:34.714 --> 01:11:37.714
I pray that it goes well with you in spirit, soul, and body.

237
01:11:38.714 --> 01:11:42.714
Every aspect in our being and in our life, good.

238
01:11:43.714 --> 01:11:45.714
Does it mean that it is always easy? Nah.

239
01:11:46.714 --> 01:11:47.714
But still good.

240
01:11:47.714 --> 01:11:54.714
God of heaven, great and mighty God, you hold fast to your covenant with the people who love you and obey you.

241
01:11:55.714 --> 01:11:57.714
God is faithful to His promises.

242
01:11:58.714 --> 01:12:02.714
He holds on to the agreements, covenant is just agreements.

243
01:12:03.714 --> 01:12:06.714
But agreements that really have value, that really have substance.

